  "title": "Woman Wins Nearly £50,000 After Bosses Mistook Medication Side Effects for Intoxication",
  "summary": "A transport manager has been awarded £49,612 by an employment tribunal after she was dismissed by her employer, which wrongly assumed she had returned from lunch under the influence of alcohol or drugs. Samantha Dallimore, who worked as a Customer Liaison Manager at AT Transport Solutions in Corby, Northamptonshire, was experiencing the effects of medication for bipolar disorder when colleagues became concerned about her behaviour at work. Medication Side Effects Mistaken for Alcohol or Drugs",
